# The Vercel CLI uploads the working directory and does NOT apply .gitignore,
# so anything that should stay off the deploy has to be listed here as well.
# Without this, `vercel` from a developer's machine ships whatever that machine
# happens to have lying around, and the deploy stops matching what a
# Git-connected build would produce.
#
# It does exclude .env* on its own — verified: OPENAI_API_KEY is absent from
# the deployed functions, so secrets in .env.local are not uploaded.

# Relevance-tuning script — developer tooling, not imported by the app.
calibrate.mjs

# The layout audit and the decks it writes. Both are for a developer checking
# slide geometry; neither is reachable from the deployed app.
#
# Leading slashes are load-bearing. These follow .gitignore's rules, where an
# unanchored `supabase/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — which
# took lib/supabase/ with it and failed the build on "Can't resolve
# './supabase/client'", a file that had been there all along.
/scripts/
/.deck-audit/

# Migrations are run by hand in the Supabase SQL editor, never by the app.
/supabase/
